# Rank 1504 / CVE-2026-42074: OpenClaude's Bash and PowerShell tools exposed
# dangerouslyDisableSandbox in the model-facing input schema, so a model-
# controlled tool_use payload could set the flag directly and run its command
# outside the sandbox (CWE-284, CWE-306): shouldUseSandbox() in
# src/tools/BashTool/shouldUseSandbox.ts returned false -- no sandbox -- when
# input.dangerouslyDisableSandbox is set and policy allows unsandboxed
# commands, and nothing distinguished the model's tool input from a trusted
# internal caller. The fixing commit ("fix:
# require trusted approval for sandbox override (#778)"): the schema gains an
# internal _dangerouslyDisableSandboxApproved field that the model-facing
# schema omits, and the override now requires both the flag and the approval.

#
# ATTENTION, vocabulary gap. The weakness is not a taint flow: a security-
# critical switch is controlled by model-facing input with no trust check on
# the path. The sanctioned route for that shape is an issue review concept
# with a binding, exactly as VYQL-AUTH-091 / code.RunTestsAutoApproval-
# ExecutesCode does for run_tests-style tools that execute project code while
# declaring automatic approval. What cannot be written from documentation
# alone is the discriminator: a binding on the mere presence of
# dangerouslyDisableSandbox in a tool schema fires on every Claude-Code-style
# agent -- the flag is the de-facto documented BashTool surface and most
# clones gate it with a permission callback or approval mode living outside
# the schema file -- while keying on openclaude's own
# _dangerouslyDisableSandboxApproved neighbour detects this repository's fix,
# not the weakness. Measured on the real code: scanning src/tools/BashTool at
# the vulnerable revision and the fixed revision report one unrelated finding each
# (VYQL-CRY-003 weak random in sedEditParser.ts:304), nothing on
# shouldUseSandbox, the schema, or the override path; the fixed-revision directory scan
# at the parent reports 557 injection-family findings, none touching the
# sandbox decision. No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry: nothing here is a mechanical
# engine change; the missing piece is a trustworthy way to state "this
# schema field is settable by the untrusted party and gates a security
# boundary", which is vocabulary design with a precision question attached.
# No definition change shipped. Spec cve_rank1504 records the model-settable
# override and the approval-gated form, both asserting reject VYQL-AUTH-091.

test "rank1504: the model sets the sandbox override directly"
  lang javascript
  file src/tools/BashTool/shouldUseSandbox.ts
  reject VYQL-AUTH-091
  code
  ```
  type SandboxInput = {
    command?: string
    dangerouslyDisableSandbox?: boolean;
  };

  export function shouldUseSandbox(input: Partial<SandboxInput>): boolean {
    if (input.dangerouslyDisableSandbox && SandboxManager.areUnsandboxedCommandsAllowed()) {
      return false;
    }
    return true;
  }

  namespace SandboxManager {
    export function areUnsandboxedCommandsAllowed(): boolean {
      return true;
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1504: the fixed revision requires the internal approval marker"
  lang javascript
  file src/tools/BashTool/shouldUseSandbox.ts
  reject VYQL-AUTH-091
  code
  ```
  type SandboxInput = {
    command?: string
    dangerouslyDisableSandbox?: boolean;
    _dangerouslyDisableSandboxApproved?: boolean;
  };

  export function shouldUseSandbox(input: Partial<SandboxInput>): boolean {
    if (
      input.dangerouslyDisableSandbox &&
      input._dangerouslyDisableSandboxApproved &&
      SandboxManager.areUnsandboxedCommandsAllowed()
    ) {
      return false;
    }
    return true;
  }

  namespace SandboxManager {
    export function areUnsandboxedCommandsAllowed(): boolean {
      return true;
    }
  }
  ```
